""0	CHAR	0
	1949
<The majority of people living in Viet Nam have learned about the Resistance war against French and American from a very young age. And most of us know that its a glorious victory that we always proud of. But the progress from being ruled by colonist to independence is rough journey and also requires a lot of efforts from many leaders. And one the most admired general that leads Vietnam to independence is General Vo Nguyen Giap. He was born in August 25th, 1911. Living in a family with strong patriotic tradition, he was inspired by his father named Vo Quang Nghiem - a great Confucian scholar. After getting kicked out of Quốc Học – Huế High School for the Gifted for organizing a rebellion, he decided to be a History teacher at Thang Long primary school from 1931 to 1939. During this time, he also worked as a journalist and a revolutionist and inspired a lot of people to join the resistance war by writing news for Tiếng Dân and Le Travail. Then, in 1940, he joined the Communist Party of Indochina and established Vietnam Propaganda Liberation Army in 1944 with only 34 people. And in 1945, he led an armed forces to take over the current government during the Agust Revolution. Two years later, he got promoted as the first general and Commander-in-Chief of the Vietnam's People Army. In this position, he had helped the army won many battles, including the Battle of Dien Bien Phu by planning perfect strategy and making wise decisions. Even after the war ended, he helped contributing to military strategies and played a senior leadership role in directing the Ho Chi Minh Campaign, leading to the liberation of South Vietnam and national unification. Since the late 1980s onward, he gradually stepped back from leadership roles, but continued contributing insights on defense, history, and science. Sadly, in 2013, he passed away at the age of 103, but his dedication to the country will live forever in citizens' heart.
|3,1,0,0,1,0,1759212173,>1948
|<"The majority of people living in Viet Nam have learned about the Resistance war against French and American from a very young age. And most of us know that its a glorious victory that we always proud of. But the progress from being ruled by colonist to independence is rough journey and also requires a lot of efforts from many leaders. And one the most admired general that leads Vietnam to independence is General Vo Nguyen Giap. He was born in August 25th, 1911. Living in a family with 
|<strong patriotic tradition, he was inspired by his father named Vo Quang Nghiem - a great Confucian scholar. After getting kicked out of Quốc Học – Huế High School for the Gifted for organizing a rebellion, he decided to be a History teacher at Thang Long primary school from 1931 to 1939. During this time, he also worked as a journalist and a revolutionist and inspired a lot of people to join the resistance war by writing news for Tiếng Dân and Le Travail. Then, in 1940, he 
|<joined the Communist Party of Indochina and established Vietnam Propaganda Liberation Army in 1944 with only 34 people. And in 1945, he led an armed forces to take over the current government during the Agust Revolution. Two years later, he got promoted as the first general and Commander-in-Chief of the Vietnam's People Army. In this position, he had helped the army won many battles, including the Battle of Dien Bien Phu by planning perfect strategy and making wise decisions. Even afte
|<r the war ended, he helped contributing to military strategies and played a senior leadership role in directing the Ho Chi Minh Campaign, leading to the liberation of South Vietnam and national unification. Since the late 1980s onward, he gradually stepped back from leadership roles, but continued contributing insights on defense, history, and science. Sadly, in 2013, he passed away at the age of 103, but his dedication to the country will live forever in citizens' heart."
